id: pm-session-reference-recovery
title: Session reference receipts advertise unsupported get --brief recovery
description: "While verifying live SDK read-envelope observability, the session receipt restore_reference_with command pm get <item-id> --brief was checked against the current CLI. get refuses --brief with unknown_option; its accepted projection spelling is --depth brief. Update the shared SDK session-reference recovery contract and add executable grammar coverage instead of only asserting the recovery string."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,output-budget,recovery,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T06:39:45.840Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T07:28:34.552Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "Every advertised session-reference restore command is accepted by current CLI contracts; A sandboxed session repeat can be restored using its advertised command; Public receipt literal types, docs and generated surface remain aligned."
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: A repeated session item can be restored by executing the command advertised in its public receipt against the current CLI grammar.
